  context="Socrates deals with the two parts of the old slander: that he studies nature, and that he teaches for money. Gorgias, Prodicus and Hippias were famous sophists; Evenus of Paros, mentioned here, was a minor one who charged five minae, a large sum.",
  plain="Socrates says: you have all seen Aristophanes' comedy, but none of you has ever heard me talk about the heavens. Nor am I a paid teacher. I would be proud to have the sophists' skill, but I do not have it.",
